6. Section 6 arithmetic: 'VSI works in the worst case' (3 n0 K vs 20 n0 K)
==============================================================================
  Ratio of guarantees: 3 n0 K / (n0 K / 0.05) = 0.15 < 0.2.  This compares UPPER BOUNDS;
  chained imitation's actual cost can be far below n0 K / eps (see report B5).
  Extra human effort not in 3 n0 K: verifications, post-mortem reads (<= K/b), audits.
  With an imitated verifier at eps_V = 5%: ~20 K_V verifications of cost c_V task steps each.
  VSI stays under a fifth of 20 n0 K iff 3 n0 K + 20 c_V K_V + c_PM K <= 4 n0 K:
    n0 = 20, K_V/K = 0.5, post-mortem cost 0.0 steps: needs c_V <= 2.00 task steps
    n0 = 20, K_V/K = 0.5, post-mortem cost 0.1 steps: needs c_V <= 1.99 task steps
    n0 = 20, K_V/K = 1.0, post-mortem cost 0.0 steps: needs c_V <= 1.00 task steps
    n0 = 20, K_V/K = 1.0, post-mortem cost 0.1 steps: needs c_V <= 0.99 task steps
    n0 = 40, K_V/K = 0.5, post-mortem cost 0.0 steps: needs c_V <= 4.00 task steps
    n0 = 40, K_V/K = 0.5, post-mortem cost 0.1 steps: needs c_V <= 3.99 task steps
    n0 = 40, K_V/K = 1.0, post-mortem cost 0.0 steps: needs c_V <= 2.00 task steps
    n0 = 40, K_V/K = 1.0, post-mortem cost 0.1 steps: needs c_V <= 1.99 task steps

