7. Imitated verifier when the verdict needs problem-specific knowledge
==============================================================================
  Hidden-insight class (note.md Theorem 3), each of m problems seen once (T = m).
  An unlocated insight problem's run fails; V_H rejects it; V' (posterior Pr[insight] = eta < 1/2)
  accepts it.  So unasked false acceptances = (1 - beta) * (#insight problems) ~ (1 - beta) eta m.
  Output failure <= eps needs beta >= 1 - eps/eta, i.e. almost every notebook verified.
    eta = 0.05, eps = 0.01: beta >= 0.80; verifications >= 0.80 m; K_V/eps >=  28.6 m  (vs T = m verifying everything)
    eta = 0.05, eps = 0.02: beta >= 0.60; verifications >= 0.60 m; K_V/eps >=  14.3 m  (vs T = m verifying everything)
    eta = 0.10, eps = 0.01: beta >= 0.90; verifications >= 0.90 m; K_V/eps >=  46.9 m  (vs T = m verifying everything)
    eta = 0.10, eps = 0.02: beta >= 0.80; verifications >= 0.80 m; K_V/eps >=  23.4 m  (vs T = m verifying everything)
    eta = 0.10, eps = 0.05: beta >= 0.50; verifications >= 0.50 m; K_V/eps >=   9.4 m  (vs T = m verifying everything)
    eta = 0.20, eps = 0.01: beta >= 0.95; verifications >= 0.95 m; K_V/eps >=  72.2 m  (vs T = m verifying everything)
    eta = 0.20, eps = 0.02: beta >= 0.90; verifications >= 0.90 m; K_V/eps >=  36.1 m  (vs T = m verifying everything)
    eta = 0.20, eps = 0.05: beta >= 0.75; verifications >= 0.75 m; K_V/eps >=  14.4 m  (vs T = m verifying everything)
  Theorem 6 is not contradicted (K_V grows with m), but 'about K_V/eps verifications, for
  any number of problems' saves nothing here: imitation pays only if verdicts are generic
  (e.g. line-by-line proof checking) or problems recur.
